## Recent Infrastructure Enhancements (October 6, 2025 - Continued)

### 3. Async gRPC Server Base Class ✅
**Component:** proto/grpc_base.py
**Type:** Infrastructure enhancement
**Commit:** 412f8ec

**Changes:**
- Added GRPCAsyncServerBase class for async/await server patterns
- Provides grpc.aio.Server support for modern async implementations
- Maintains consistent keepalive configuration with sync version
- Implements proper async lifecycle management (start, stop, wait_for_termination)
- Template pattern for subclass servicer registration

**Impact:**
- ✅ Enables modern async/await server implementations
- ✅ Better integration with asyncio-based services
- ✅ Improved concurrency handling for I/O-bound operations
- ✅ Consistent behavior with existing sync servers
- ✅ Maintains production-tested keepalive settings

**Technical Details:**
- Uses grpc.aio.server() for async server creation
- Same server options as GRPCServerBase (60s keepalive, 4MB messages)
- Graceful shutdown with configurable grace period
- Shutdown event for coordination
- Full async context manager support

**Use Cases:**
- Services requiring high concurrency with async I/O
- Integration with existing asyncio-based codebases
- Modern Python async/await patterns
- Better resource utilization for I/O-bound workloads

**Code Quality:**
- 75 lines of clean, well-documented code
- Follows existing patterns from GRPCServerBase
- Maintains backward compatibility
- No breaking changes to existing code

This enhancement completes the gRPC infrastructure foundation by providing both synchronous and asynchronous server base classes, giving developers full flexibility in choosing the most appropriate implementation pattern for their specific use case.

